// Title: Renamed BrowserCore.EXE Execution
// Sigma ID: 8a4519e8-e64a-40b6-ae85-ba8ad2177559
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Max Altgelt (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-06-02 | Modified: 2023-02-03
// ATT&CK: credential-access, stealth, T1528, T1036.003
// Description: Detects process creation with a renamed BrowserCore.exe (used to extract Azure tokens)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/mariuszbit/status/1531631015139102720
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_browsercore.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "BrowserCore.exe" and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\BrowserCore.exe"))
